From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:43:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Declare _WorldSpaceReferencePosition as float3

It is set with SetVector and used as a position by the
SEPARATE_LOD_RANGE_CULLING Evaluate kernels (scatters culled around the craft
rather than the camera), but was declared as a float, so only its x
component reached the shader.
---
 Assets/Shaders/Scatters/ScatterParams.cginc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Assets/Shaders/Scatters/ScatterParams.cginc b/Assets/Shaders/Scatters/ScatterParams.cginc
index a4d1d58..bb4dd0e 100644
--- a/Assets/Shaders/Scatters/ScatterParams.cginc
+++ b/Assets/Shaders/Scatters/ScatterParams.cginc
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ float _CullLimit;
 // Range before cutting off entirely
 float _MaxRange;
 
-float _WorldSpaceReferencePosition;
+float3 _WorldSpaceReferencePosition;
 
 // Range before scatters begin to cut off
 float _RangeFadeStart;
